<edge source="ai_buildout_backlash::policy_uncertainty_ai" target="china_tech_rivalry::regulatory_tightness" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising uncertainty about AI rules and data‑centre policy leads regulators to impose clearer, more prescriptive and precautionary measures (moratoria, licensing, compliance mandates) to reduce perceived risk and restore control.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_backlash</data>
  <data key="d40">china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_buildout_backlash::policy_uncertainty_ai" target="global_market_repricing::interest_rate_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">An increase in regulatory and policy uncertainty around AI causes markets to downgrade near‑term growth and prompt expectations that central banks will delay or slow further tightening, lowering market‑implied future policy rate paths.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_backlash</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_buildout_backlash::policy_uncertainty_ai" target="russia_ukraine_war::transatl_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Rising uncertainty and divergent national approaches to AI export controls and data‑centre regulation produce bilateral disputes and slow coordination on export/dual‑use rules and intelligence sharing, directly eroding allied policy alignment and burden‑sharing.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-12 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_backlash</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_buildout_backlash::policy_uncertainty_ai" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Unclear or changing rules on AI‑enabled systems and data exports generate delays and legal reviews in export licensing and procurement approvals, directly slowing the authorization and shipment of AI‑enabled munitions and sensors to Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_backlash</data>
