<edge source="us_iran_escalation::sanctions_pressure_level" target="ai_buildout_backlash::policy_uncertainty_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.8</data>
  <data key="d37">Expansion or threat of targeted sanctions on technology exports and firms creates immediate ambiguity about permissible suppliers, cross‑border data flows, and compliance obligations, increasing uncertainty about future rules governing AI and data‑centre activity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_buildout_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_escalation::sanctions_pressure_level" target="china_tech_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Intensified sanctions against Iran prompt the US and partners to expand export-licensing rules, tighten secondary-sanctions compliance, and broaden controlled item lists—measures that are applied to flows involving Chinese firms and thus raise outbound/export control stringency.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_escalation::sanctions_pressure_level" target="global_market_repricing::interest_rate_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader or tighter sanctions raise the risk of supply disruptions and dislocation in trade/finance, leading markets to price faster or higher central‑bank tightening to counter imported inflation and financial fragmentation.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="us_iran_escalation::sanctions_pressure_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::transatl_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Escalating, extraterritorial sanctions on Iran provoke disagreement among transatlantic partners over exposure, legal risk, and economic costs, producing splits in policy alignment and burden‑sharing that weaken coordinated responses toward Russia/Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">us_iran_escalation</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
