<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" target="china_tech_rivalry::diplomatic_tension" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained Western arms flows to Ukraine provoke sharper rhetorical responses, diplomatic countermeasures, and closer operational alignment between Russia and China, which in turn elicit punitive measures and heightened bilateral friction between Western capitals and Beijing.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">china_tech_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" target="global_market_repricing::nominal_govt_bond_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">A sustained uptick in arms and munitions deliveries forces governments to accelerate procurement spending and financing, increasing near‑term sovereign debt issuance and pushing yields higher.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" target="us_iran_escalation::sanctions_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased transfers of Iranian-origin weapons or dual-use materiel to Russia for use in Ukraine trigger U.S. and allied secondary sanctions and expanded listings against the Iranian suppliers, shippers and financial facilitators directly tied to those flows.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" target="us_iran_escalation::kinetic_operations_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A rise in observable arms shipments and transits linked to Iran prompts U.S. kinetic interdiction operations and strikes against shipment routes, storage nodes or proxy networks in the Middle East to disrupt transfers and deter further deliveries.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_escalation</data>
</edge>
