  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Stronger perceived deterrence lowers the probability of conflict escalation and safe‑haven demand, supporting growth and inflation expectations and thus raising market‑implied future policy‑rate expectations.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_repricing</data>
