<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::state_inv_priority" target="ai_buildout_backlash::capital_flows_equities" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">When the state directs capital, offers subsidies or guarantees to strategic tech and AI firms, it directly injects capital and reduces perceived project risk, which attracts additional private equity and portfolio investment into AI‑linked equities.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_buildout_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::state_inv_priority" target="global_market_repricing::headline_inflation_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Sustained increases in state‑directed investment raise demand for commodities and intermediate goods (metals, energy, semiconductors inputs), tightening global supply/demand balances and lifting headline goods prices.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::state_inv_priority" target="us_iran_escalation::chokepoint_vulnerability" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.55</data>
  <data key="d37">Increased Chinese state‑directed investment in regional ports, terminals, and logistics infrastructure expands Beijing's commercial and operational footprint at maritime chokepoints, producing new ownership, access patterns and dependencies that raise the risk of contestation or interdiction in a US–Iran crisis.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_escalation</data>
</edge>
