<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" target="ai_buildout_backlash::policy_uncertainty_ai" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.85</data>
  <data key="d37">Broadening or tightening outbound export controls creates immediate ambiguity about which AI components, cloud services, or data flows will be allowed, forcing firms to reassess compliance and build contingency plans, which raises measured policy uncertainty about AI and data‑centre rules.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">ai_buildout_backlash</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" target="global_market_repricing::interest_rate_expect" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">A sudden tightening of export/outbound controls disrupts trade and investment flows and slows near‑term growth prospects, leading market participants to lower their expectations for future policy rates.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" target="global_market_repricing::nominal_govt_bond_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">+</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">Broader and stricter export controls raise country‑specific geopolitical and counterparty risks, prompting capital reallocation and higher sovereign risk premia that push up benchmark government bond yields.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">global_market_repricing</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" target="russia_ukraine_war::arms_supply_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">3</data>
  <data key="d36">0.7</data>
  <data key="d37">Tighter Chinese export and outbound controls on semiconductors, sensors and drone components directly restrict the ability of China‑based manufacturers and brokers to supply or re‑export key parts used in Russian UAVs, guidance kits and munitions, reducing the rate of arms and munitions delivered into Russia's procurement chains.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" target="us_iran_escalation::escalation_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.65</data>
  <data key="d37">Stricter Chinese outbound controls on dual‑use components and surveillance/communications gear reduce Iran's near‑term access to technology used for targeting, ISR, and guidance, degrading its ability to mount or sustain proximate hostile actions and thereby lowering escalation pressure.</data>
  <data key="d38">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_escalation</data>
</edge>
<edge source="china_tech_rivalry::export_control_stringenc" target="us_iran_escalation::sanctions_pressure_level" id="0">
  <data key="d28">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d34">-</data>
  <data key="d29">2</data>
  <data key="d36">0.6</data>
  <data key="d37">If China demonstrably tightens and enforces outbound export controls on technology flows to Iran or known intermediary firms, US policy makers face reduced political and evidentiary pressure to expand sanctions, lowering aggregate sanctions intensity.</data>
  <data key="d38">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d39">china_tech_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d40">us_iran_escalation</data>
</edge>
